That little sucker growled at me.


00:21:23.158 --> 00:21:25.410
You piss on that rug, you're dead.


00:21:25.536 --> 00:21:27.037
Hey!


00:21:29.373 --> 00:21:31.834
He was just kidding! Come back!


00:21:31.959 --> 00:21:33.585
Meanies.


00:21:33.710 --> 00:21:37.381
That dog is weird. He just growled at me
for no good reason.


00:21:37.506 --> 00:21:40.926
I said I liked cats.
I wasn't talking about the musical.


00:21:41.051 --> 00:21:43.512
This little dog is harmless.
Chicken.


00:21:43.637 --> 00:21:46.682
Don't worry, he'll come back.
He knows there's food here.


00:21:46.807 --> 00:21:48.475
You wanna find him?


00:21:48.600 --> 00:21:51.436
- I wanted to sleep with him.
- You were sleeping with me!


00:21:51.562 --> 00:21:54.439
She was gonna make love to me
and then sleep in your bed.


00:21:54.565 --> 00:21:56.024
That's Ok.


00:21:56.149 --> 00:22:00.070
I see cancer patients every Thursday.
That's my charity work for the week.


00:22:00.195 --> 00:22:03.699
Oh! Funny!


00:22:03.824 --> 00:22:06.368
The folks got jokes tonight.
You all want some?


00:22:13.625 --> 00:22:16.920
Here, pup. Where are you?


00:22:17.045 --> 00:22:19.715
- You see him?
- Uh-uh.


00:22:20.757 --> 00:22:22.843
This is bringing me back memories


00:22:22.968 --> 00:22:26.221
from Ghost in the Graveyard.
Remember? When we were ten?


00:22:26.346 --> 00:22:28.223
I don't remember that.


00:22:28.348 --> 00:22:33.562
- Yeah, you were too cool back then.
- I'm still too cool.


00:22:33.729 --> 00:22:36.106
- Right.
- Over there. There he is.


00:22:36.231 --> 00:22:38.400
(Pup whines)


00:22:38.525 --> 00:22:42.613
Hey, pup, there you are.
There you are! Come here.


00:22:43.989 --> 00:22:46.450
(Snarling)


00:22:50.287 --> 00:22:52.664
(Snarling)


00:22:57.377 --> 00:22:59.671
(Barks)


00:23:00.964 --> 00:23:02.883
Sara!


00:23:10.641 --> 00:23:12.935
You Ok?


00:23:15.062 --> 00:23:16.939
Here.


00:23:18.023 --> 00:23:19.650
(John) Ok?


00:23:19.775 --> 00:23:21.652
(Low growl)


00:23:26.782 --> 00:23:29.326
It bit me.


00:23:29.493 --> 00:23:31.578
All right, you're Ok.


00:23:31.703 --> 00:23:34.790
You're Ok. Come on, let's go.


00:23:34.915 --> 00:23:36.875
It just attacked you, unprovoked?


00:23:37.000 --> 00:23:39.920
Yeah. Came out of nowhere.


00:23:41.088 --> 00:23:43.382
It was probably just protecting
its young


00:23:43.549 --> 00:23:48.262
but the rules say you gotta treat
any bite by an unknown animal


00:23:48.387 --> 00:23:51.181
as a possible rabies infection.


00:23:51.306 --> 00:23:55.811
But listen, you will not get rabies.
I know what I'm talking about.


00:23:55.936 --> 00:23:59.064
There isn't a single case
of somebody who's gone through


00:23:59.189 --> 00:24:03.026
a proper post-exposure treatment
who's then contracted the disease.


00:24:03.193 --> 00:24:06.864
Isn't that where they gotta stick
a bunch of needles under your skin?


00:24:07.030 --> 00:24:09.241
(Matt) It's a little simpler than that.


00:24:09.366 --> 00:24:12.452
- A little simpler?
- I think we should get the plane ready.


00:24:12.619 --> 00:24:16.832
- You wanna leave?
- We should get Sara to a doctor.


00:24:16.957 --> 00:24:22.171
Remember when I got that rabies shot
cos of that bat in the Bahamas?


00:24:22.296 --> 00:24:24.673
You don't have to start right away.


00:24:24.798 --> 00:24:29.178
- You really don't, if you're feeling Ok.
- Is that true?


00:24:30.429 --> 00:24:33.849
As long as you have your first shot
within a week, yes.


00:24:34.016 --> 00:24:37.102
But... there's no pressure.


00:24:37.227 --> 00:24:40.397
Well, then I'm cool.
I'll be fine, you guys.


00:24:40.522 --> 00:24:42.024
- She's fine.
- Sara?


00:24:42.149 --> 00:24:46.612
Mattie, the point of this weekend
was for you to live a little,


00:24:46.778 --> 00:24:49.531
so don't use this as an excuse.
That's bullshit.


00:24:49.698 --> 00:24:53.994
Yeah, it's true, I'm fine. I mean, really.
It was scary!


00:24:54.161 --> 00:24:58.290
Nothing that a little drinking can't cure.


00:24:58.457 --> 00:25:01.877
Could someone give me a drink?
I need a drink.


00:25:02.002 --> 00:25:06.131
- Are you sure?
- Yeah. Sure I'm sure.


00:25:08.717 --> 00:25:12.387
(Thunderclap)


00:25:44.002 --> 00:25:47.172
(Nikki) What are you thinking about?


00:25:52.469 --> 00:25:56.056
There was this company
who leased some land


00:25:56.223 --> 00:25:59.935
on the other side of the island,
a couple of miles away.


00:26:00.102 --> 00:26:05.065
Anyway, they built a compound
for training dogs.


00:26:05.232 --> 00:26:08.735
When I was little, my uncle
used to walk me over there


00:26:08.902 --> 00:26:12.155
and we'd play with all
the little puppies.


00:26:12.322 --> 00:26:15.576
I think that's when I decided
I wanted to be a vet.


00:26:17.995 --> 00:26:20.038
About a year ago...


00:26:21.623 --> 00:26:24.710
...one of the dogs got rabies.


00:26:24.835 --> 00:26:28.964
It started spreading
and all the dogs got it,


00:26:29.131 --> 00:26:32.217
and my uncle told me
they had to put them down.


00:26:34.052 --> 00:26:37.139
- That's horrible.
- Mmm.


00:26:39.266 --> 00:26:42.477
So I assumed
they had been killed, but...


00:26:46.481 --> 00:26:49.234
...after seeing that dog today...


00:26:51.236 --> 00:26:54.781
So you think some of them survived?


00:26:54.948 --> 00:26:57.284
That's just it.


00:26:57.451 --> 00:27:01.580
If they had rabies and escaped, they
would've been dead a long time ago.


00:27:03.248 --> 00:27:06.543
In dogs, rabies is always fatal.


00:27:11.632 --> 00:27:13.675
So, what are you saying?


00:27:15.260 --> 00:27:17.304
I don't know.


00:27:36.698 --> 00:27:38.534
(Clears throat)


00:27:42.829 --> 00:27:45.040
Oh!


00:27:45.207 --> 00:27:47.417
Sorry. I didn't see you.


00:27:47.584 --> 00:27:49.920
What are you doing?


00:27:50.087 --> 00:27:52.130
I couldn't sleep.


00:27:55.092 --> 00:27:57.970
- You?
- Me, neither.


00:28:00.764 --> 00:28:03.058
You look like an angel.


00:28:33.172 --> 00:28:35.716
Ow! Damn it!


00:28:35.841 --> 00:28:38.218
Easy, tiger.


00:28:38.343 --> 00:28:40.971
Go away.


00:28:44.391 --> 00:28:46.476
Go away.


00:29:01.575 --> 00:29:04.912
(Thunder rumbles)


00:29:20.260 --> 00:29:23.055
So, how about doing
some swimming today?


00:29:23.180 --> 00:29:26.058
Maybe hang out by the dock?


00:29:26.183 --> 00:29:28.477
Maybe when your leg feels better?


00:29:30.145 --> 00:29:31.897
I'm fine.


00:29:34.525 --> 00:29:37.194
How did I wind up dating
an outdoorsy type?


00:29:37.319 --> 00:29:39.196
(Voices echo)


00:29:39.321 --> 00:29:43.158
(Nikki) I don't know. I think it's
a lot better than living in a library.


00:29:43.283 --> 00:29:47.829
(Noah) I'm outdoorsy as long as
beautiful women in thongs are involved.


00:29:47.955 --> 00:29:51.667
Do you ever get tired
of making an ass of yourself?


00:29:51.792 --> 00:29:54.711
Not really. I figure
it's a part of my charm.


00:29:55.963 --> 00:29:59.132
Yo. Excuse me.


00:29:59.258 --> 00:30:01.301
I'm still hungry.


00:30:02.427 --> 00:30:04.930
- Knock yourself out.
- (Matt) I'll make more.


00:30:05.055 --> 00:30:07.224
(Noah) No, that's cool.


00:30:09.017 --> 00:30:11.520
- Morning, guys.
- Good morning.


00:30:12.688 --> 00:30:14.773
Boys and their toys.


00:30:14.898 --> 00:30:18.318
I thought I'd take a walk in the woods
and find something to shoot.


00:30:18.443 --> 00:30:20.445
I hope you mean something inanimate.


00:30:20.571 --> 00:30:24.491
- Gosh, no, I thought I'd hunt for Bambi.
- (Matt) Just checking.


00:30:24.616 --> 00:30:28.829
I'm gonna come with you. I haven't
been around the island for years.


00:30:28.954 --> 00:30:31.582
- You guys wanna come?
- Noah, come on.


00:30:31.707 --> 00:30:34.585
Yeah. Yeah, why not?


00:30:34.710 --> 00:30:37.713
Enjoy your breakfast.


00:30:40.883 --> 00:30:44.636
Actually, I think I'm gonna stay here.


00:30:44.761 --> 00:30:47.306
I'm not keen on that dog running around.


00:30:47.431 --> 00:30:51.977
- Ok. We'll be careful.
- Keep him away from Thumper, too.


00:30:52.102 --> 00:30:54.188
(Noah) Come on.


00:31:04.990 --> 00:31:08.285
No deer. No droppings.


00:31:12.956 --> 00:31:15.042
You hear anything?


00:31:16.543 --> 00:31:18.921
No.


00:31:19.046 --> 00:31:21.757
It makes you wonder
where all the animals are.


00:31:21.882 --> 00:31:25.135
Are you guys trying
to freak me out or something?


00:31:25.260 --> 00:31:29.223
Is this like a game you play?
What?


00:31:29.348 --> 00:31:32.684
- No, I'm serious.
- He's referring to inanimate animals.


00:31:35.437 --> 00:31:38.857
You think Sara is feeling Ok?


00:31:38.982 --> 00:31:41.443
I hope so.


00:31:41.568 --> 00:31:44.154
- She's looking pretty good these days.
- Don't.


00:31:44.279 --> 00:31:46.156
- What?
- Don't go there.


00:31:46.281 --> 00:31:48.158
Why not?


00:31:48.283 --> 00:31:52.246
She's obviously into me, so why
shouldn't I just go for it?


00:31:52.371 --> 00:31:54.748
- Really?
- Yeah.


00:31:55.832 --> 00:31:58.043
Because I've seen
how you treat women.


00:32:00.546 --> 00:32:02.631
Because you're good
at saving them


00:32:02.756 --> 00:32:05.551
doesn't always mean I'm the one
that ruins them.


00:32:07.845 --> 00:32:11.515
- Brother in love.
- It's all right, man.


00:32:12.182 --> 00:32:15.185
- Are you feeling all right?
- Yeah.


00:32:15.310 --> 00:32:17.396
Are you sure?


00:32:18.438 --> 00:32:20.524
I made out with John.


00:32:21.692 --> 00:32:25.654
- So that's what's bothering you?
- Kind of, yeah.


00:32:25.779 --> 00:32:27.698
- Why?
- Nice.


00:32:27.823 --> 00:32:32.870
I don't know. I guess I thought
the rabies was settling in.


00:32:32.995 --> 00:32:36.748
Very funny.
No, actually, I feel fine.


00:32:36.874 --> 00:32:41.211
I feel great. I've got like this
adrenaline inside.


00:32:41.336 --> 00:32:43.839
From John kissing you?


00:32:43.964 --> 00:32:46.049
- Maybe.
- Well, might as well.


00:32:46.175 --> 00:32:51.013
- You've liked him since you were 14.
- How did you know?


00:32:51.138 --> 00:32:53.974
Who doesn't know that?
Everybody knows.


00:32:54.099 --> 00:32:55.851
Oh, really?


00:32:55.976 --> 00:32:59.813
Ok, then I hate everybody
right now.


00:33:05.319 --> 00:33:07.404
(John hollers) Any day, Mcknight!


00:33:07.529 --> 00:33:09.781
Can a brother not get
some alone time?


00:33:09.907 --> 00:33:11.992
Damn!


00:33:19.666 --> 00:33:21.752
(Low growl)


00:33:24.129 --> 00:33:26.215
(Growling)


00:33:42.814 --> 00:33:44.733
Nice doggy.


00:33:46.443 --> 00:33:48.529
Nice doggy.


00:33:51.823 --> 00:33:53.909
Good boy.


00:33:55.786 --> 00:33:58.038
Oh!


00:33:58.163 --> 00:34:03.210
Ok, Ok...
It's fine. It's fine.


00:34:03.335 --> 00:34:05.796
(Growling)


00:34:07.381 --> 00:34:10.676
John! Matt! Hey!


00:34:19.601 --> 00:34:21.687
Oh! Oh!


00:34:23.897 --> 00:34:25.649
Oh!


00:34:25.774 --> 00:34:30.279
- What happened?
- What are you doing?


00:34:30.404 --> 00:34:33.490
The dogs on this island
are not friendly!


00:34:33.615 --> 00:34:36.159
- You afraid of a dog?
- No, dogs, man. Plural.


00:34:36.285 --> 00:34:38.871
- How many?
- Three, but it sounded like more.


00:34:38.996 --> 00:34:40.873
(Rustling in undergrowth)


00:34:40.998 --> 00:34:43.500
You hear that?


00:34:43.625 --> 00:34:45.711
(Rustling)


00:34:48.881 --> 00:34:50.966
You believe me now?


00:34:53.135 --> 00:34:55.721
(All) Oh!


00:34:55.846 --> 00:34:58.974
They don't want you here.


00:34:59.099 --> 00:35:01.310
The dogs, they don't want you here.


00:35:07.107 --> 00:35:10.611
(Man yells and dog snarls)


00:35:10.736 --> 00:35:13.197
(Man yells) Help!


00:35:20.662 --> 00:35:22.206
- Get back!
- We gotta help him!


00:35:22.831 --> 00:35:25.375
(Barking and snarling)


00:35:33.467 --> 00:35:35.677
What's up?


00:35:40.224 --> 00:35:41.683
Nothing.


00:35:52.986 --> 00:35:55.364
(Indistinct chatter)


00:35:57.157 --> 00:35:58.825
(Whispers) The house.


00:35:59.701 --> 00:36:01.995
- (Nikki) Hey!
- (Whispers) Go to the house.


00:36:04.665 --> 00:36:06.542
- What?
- Here they come.


00:36:06.667 --> 00:36:08.585
What?


00:36:09.169 --> 00:36:10.712
Run!


00:36:10.838 --> 00:36:13.257
- Run to the house!
- Oh, my God! Run!


00:36:13.382 --> 00:36:15.759
(Matt) Run! Hurry up!


00:36:18.262 --> 00:36:22.266
Come on, you guys!
Hurry up!


00:36:24.309 --> 00:36:25.894
Hey!


00:36:28.146 --> 00:36:30.107
Mattie, no!


00:36:43.203 --> 00:36:45.080
(Echoing scream)


00:36:56.049 --> 00:36:57.968
(Snarls)


00:37:18.405 --> 00:37:20.699
This ought to be fun.


00:37:27.915 --> 00:37:29.917
- Argh! Argh!
- Damn!


00:37:30.042 --> 00:37:32.419
Damn it! Son of a bitch!


00:37:32.544 --> 00:37:35.214
God, I'm so sorry, Nikki.


00:37:37.925 --> 00:37:39.927
That's Ok.


00:37:42.387 --> 00:37:44.681
For all I know,
you could've saved my life.


00:37:44.806 --> 00:37:48.977
I don't know if I'm the life-saving kind.
I couldn't save that guy in the woods.


00:37:49.102 --> 00:37:52.648
- I thought we were the only ones here.
- He came out of nowhere.


00:37:52.773 --> 00:37:54.858
They ripped the shit out of him.


00:37:54.983 --> 00:37:57.319
I know! Death by dog is brutal!


00:37:57.444 --> 00:38:01.156
(Matt) None of this makes sense!
There's no reason dogs could do this!


00:38:01.281 --> 00:38:03.742
These have the characteristics
of a rabid dog.


00:38:03.867 --> 00:38:07.788
- But if they had rabies, they'd be dead.
- (Noah) Then what is it?


00:38:07.913 --> 00:38:11.625
- You know that dog compound?
- The seeing-eye dog facility, yeah.


00:38:11.750 --> 00:38:14.878
What if they were actually training
attack dogs, right?


00:38:15.003 --> 00:38:19.299
A year ago they shut the compound
down because of a rabies outbreak.


00:38:19.424 --> 00:38:23.929
So, attack dogs plus a weird strain
of rabies equals what?


00:38:24.054 --> 00:38:27.140
Scary-ass Lassies, that's what!


00:38:27.266 --> 00:38:29.560
- (John) Relax.
- They don't want us here.


00:38:32.646 --> 00:38:35.315
That's what the dude in the woods said.


00:38:35.440 --> 00:38:37.568
(Matt) Twice.
(Nikki) Who cares?


00:38:37.693 --> 00:38:41.238
We need to be focusing
on getting the hell outta here!


00:38:41.363 --> 00:38:44.992
I'm in serious need of some painkillers...


00:38:45.117 --> 00:38:47.786
and there's something wrong with Sara.


00:38:47.911 --> 00:38:50.372
You feel it, don't you?


00:38:50.497 --> 00:38:53.834
- Is something wrong with you?
- It comes and goes.


00:38:53.959 --> 00:38:56.670
We've gotta be smart here,
smarter than these dogs.


00:38:56.795 --> 00:39:01.967
Everybody just shut up! You're all
driving me crazy right now! Wild dogs?


00:39:02.092 --> 00:39:04.636
Nikki's right, we gotta get outta here!


00:39:04.761 --> 00:39:07.181
Sara needs help
and we're gonna do that!


00:39:07.306 --> 00:39:11.476
But first, we'll stay in here
where it's safe, let the dogs disperse,


00:39:11.602 --> 00:39:14.479
then get in the plane
and get the hell out...


00:39:16.982 --> 00:39:19.401
(Barks)


00:39:23.238 --> 00:39:25.866
(Low growl)


00:39:39.546 --> 00:39:42.090
(Dog yelps)


00:39:48.013 --> 00:39:51.058
I don't wanna be here
any more.


00:39:53.227 --> 00:39:55.479
What do we do?


00:39:56.647 --> 00:39:58.941
We get outta here.


00:40:03.779 --> 00:40:05.989
(Matt) Ready?


00:40:13.664 --> 00:40:16.166
The dogs are on the dock.


00:40:18.460 --> 00:40:20.879
It's like they know we wanna leave.


00:40:25.884 --> 00:40:27.761
You gotta be kidding me!


00:40:27.886 --> 00:40:30.055
(John) What?


00:40:30.180 --> 00:40:33.767
- The plane's drifting away.
- It can't be. I tied it myself.


00:40:33.892 --> 00:40:35.978
Look, then.


00:40:37.354 --> 00:40:40.315
(John) Shit. If it hits the channel,
it's lost.


00:40:40.440 --> 00:40:42.818
The dogs are gone.


00:40:44.695 --> 00:40:47.239
(Noah) You guys, you guys...


00:40:47.364 --> 00:40:50.659
- I don't wanna go out there.
- You're going.


00:40:56.915 --> 00:40:59.918
You'll have to swim.
No one else can bring the plane back.


00:41:00.043 --> 00:41:02.754
- I know.
- Just give me this.


00:41:11.096 --> 00:41:15.309
For your brother being a screw-up,
he's stepping up and being a badass.


00:41:15.434 --> 00:41:19.521
I can't believe this.
They chewed through it on purpose.


00:41:19.646 --> 00:41:22.816
Listen, I don't know what the hell
is going on around here


00:41:22.941 --> 00:41:25.611
but dogs can't think like that.
They can't plan.


00:41:25.736 --> 00:41:30.032
If a dog chews through rope,
it's because dogs like chewing rope!


00:41:30.157 --> 00:41:31.992
(Noah) Come on, John.


00:41:33.911 --> 00:41:36.163
He's almost there.


00:41:44.213 --> 00:41:46.215
Shit!


00:41:49.176 --> 00:41:52.221
- Come on, swim back, man!
- (Nikki) Swim!


00:41:52.346 --> 00:41:53.847
- The dogs!
- Hurry!


00:41:56.016 --> 00:42:00.312
- Stop looking back!
- (Nikki) Swim! Swim faster!


00:42:01.188 --> 00:42:03.732
You're fine!


00:42:08.737 --> 00:42:10.781
(Barks)


00:42:14.826 --> 00:42:16.537
(Dog yelps)


00:42:16.662 --> 00:42:19.164
Bitch! Back to the house!
Come on!


00:42:19.289 --> 00:42:24.002
(Matt) Hurry up!
(Noah) Go! Go! Hurry up! Go!


00:42:24.127 --> 00:42:26.004
Run!


00:42:27.881 --> 00:42:30.259
(Noah) Go! Go! Get inside!


00:42:32.261 --> 00:42:35.305
Come on, get up the stairs!


00:42:35.430 --> 00:42:37.641
Shut the door! Shut the door!


00:42:45.899 --> 00:42:47.442
(Barking)


00:42:47.568 --> 00:42:49.987
(Hammering)


00:42:50.112 --> 00:42:53.073
(Matt) But how did the dogs
even get on the plane?


00:42:53.198 --> 00:42:56.660
I once saw a dog balance
a marshmallow on his nose.


00:43:00.789 --> 00:43:03.292
(Hammering continues)


00:43:35.157 --> 00:43:37.117
(Phone beeps)


00:43:37.242 --> 00:43:39.328
Still no service.


00:43:40.162 --> 00:43:43.707
- You're running a fever.
- I am?


00:43:43.832 --> 00:43:48.295
Don't worry, it wouldn't be rabies yet.
It could be some other kind of infection.


00:43:48.420 --> 00:43:51.006
Great.


00:43:51.131 --> 00:43:53.675
All right, pros and cons.
What are the negatives?


00:43:53.800 --> 00:43:55.636
Negatives? Well, everything.


00:43:55.761 --> 00:43:58.305
It's dangerous just trying to get
to the garage.


00:43:58.430 --> 00:44:02.643
We don't know if the car will start
or what we'll find across the island.


00:44:02.768 --> 00:44:06.605
- Whatever got that guy here.
- With our luck, he parasailed in!


00:44:06.730 --> 00:44:10.484
The compound has gotta have
some kind of communications system.


00:44:10.651 --> 00:44:13.779
Hopefully it's not equipped
with some crazy Old Yellers.


00:44:13.904 --> 00:44:17.115
Look, we can't stay here.
We gotta get off this island.


00:44:20.160 --> 00:44:22.704
Ok. Ok?


00:44:22.829 --> 00:44:24.915
Ok, damn!


00:44:40.973 --> 00:44:43.225
(Matt) All right, eeny...


00:44:43.350 --> 00:44:45.310
Meeny...


00:44:45.435 --> 00:44:48.063
Miney...


00:44:48.188 --> 00:44:49.857
I'll go.


00:44:49.982 --> 00:44:53.110
(Barking and snarling)


00:45:01.451 --> 00:45:04.454
- (John) It'll lift right off.
- I don't want you to go.


00:45:04.580 --> 00:45:09.042
- I don't want anyone to go.
- I'll be fine. I'll be really quiet.


00:45:14.506 --> 00:45:16.383
(Faint barking)


00:45:16.508 --> 00:45:18.594
(Door creaks)


00:45:30.564 --> 00:45:33.400
(Wind chimes clink)


00:45:38.030 --> 00:45:40.824
(Barking)


00:46:19.196 --> 00:46:21.240
(Pulley clanks)


00:46:46.723 --> 00:46:49.226
How much do you weigh?


00:46:50.310 --> 00:46:53.981
You know how much I weigh, baby.
You're not doing this.


00:46:54.147 --> 00:46:57.985
Speed climbing champion three years
running. I weigh 120 pounds.


00:46:58.110 --> 00:47:00.237
I could do this with my hands tied.


00:47:00.404 --> 00:47:02.781
You were injured badly.


00:47:02.948 --> 00:47:05.158
I know my limits.


00:47:05.284 --> 00:47:07.411
This cable can't support you.


00:47:07.536 --> 00:47:11.415
I know what I'm talking about.
Think about it.


00:47:14.376 --> 00:47:16.753
I mean it. Think about it.


00:47:37.399 --> 00:47:41.320
- You didn't get any on the handles?
- No, you'll be fine.


00:47:54.666 --> 00:47:57.169
- Be careful.
- Yeah.


00:48:15.020 --> 00:48:17.689
You gotta be kidding me.


00:48:17.856 --> 00:48:19.566
(Distant barking)


00:48:26.240 --> 00:48:28.116
They're here.


00:48:36.083 --> 00:48:38.210
Hurry, Nikki.


00:48:41.630 --> 00:48:44.216
(All yell) Hey! Hey!


00:48:45.676 --> 00:48:48.136
(Hollers) Hey!


00:48:48.303 --> 00:48:51.139
Dogs! Dogs!


00:48:56.645 --> 00:49:00.482
Dogs! Dogs, over here! Come on!


00:49:33.348 --> 00:49:36.018
(Engine fires once then bangs)


00:49:41.648 --> 00:49:43.233
Come on!


00:49:43.400 --> 00:49:46.069
(Engine stutters)


00:49:46.195 --> 00:49:48.238
(Engine Stutters again)


00:49:48.405 --> 00:49:51.491
Come on! Piece of shit!


00:49:51.658 --> 00:49:54.828
(Engine stutters)


00:49:55.787 --> 00:49:58.123
(Engine stutters again)


00:50:05.756 --> 00:50:07.049
(Snarls)


00:50:11.553 --> 00:50:13.555
(Barking)


00:50:55.055 --> 00:50:59.685
- (Hollers) Hey! Are you Ok?
- Yeah, I'm fine.


00:51:00.853 --> 00:51:05.065
Just seems like it's gonna be dinnertime
over here soon.


00:51:05.190 --> 00:51:07.234
Hang on.
We got something worked out.


00:51:08.485 --> 00:51:10.571
(John) Come on, guys!


00:51:10.696 --> 00:51:12.948
- Let's go!
- Yep!


00:51:13.866 --> 00:51:16.493
- Good?
- More slack! Watch yourself!


00:51:19.830 --> 00:51:23.709
- You didn't hit her this time!
- I'm gonna tie the line to the rope.


00:51:23.834 --> 00:51:25.836
- Pull it across.
- All right.


00:51:25.961 --> 00:51:28.046
Here it is!


00:51:30.883 --> 00:51:32.968
All right, pull it, pull it!


00:51:34.469 --> 00:51:36.722
(Noah) Hurry!


00:51:42.144 --> 00:51:43.937
Come on.


00:51:54.948 --> 00:51:57.784
Behind you! Jump!


00:52:06.418 --> 00:52:08.504
(Dog yelps)


00:52:09.379 --> 00:52:11.840
Come on!
Nice shot. We got one, man!


00:52:11.965 --> 00:52:15.093
Come on, pull!
Bring her in, bring her in.


00:52:17.304 --> 00:52:19.389
Get off the harness!


00:52:27.022 --> 00:52:29.107
(Distant barking)


00:52:41.245 --> 00:52:43.121
Hey.


00:52:44.623 --> 00:52:46.708
You have to talk to me.


00:52:48.168 --> 00:52:52.756
I'm not in pain but...


00:52:52.881 --> 00:52:55.133
I think I'm in trouble.


00:52:55.259 --> 00:52:58.595
- I'm so sorry for this, Sara.
- Don't be. It's not your fault.


00:52:58.720 --> 00:53:00.848
- (Matt) Yes, it is.
- Matt!


00:53:00.973 --> 00:53:02.850
It's Ok.


00:53:03.892 --> 00:53:06.144
This is Ok?


00:53:06.979 --> 00:53:09.606
None of this is Ok.


00:53:09.731 --> 00:53:13.360
We should've left this morning.
We should never even have come here.


00:53:13.485 --> 00:53:15.737
I didn't know this was supposed
to happen.


00:53:15.863 --> 00:53:18.991
Of course you didn't. Because
you don't think, you just do,


00:53:19.116 --> 00:53:22.619
only this time you dragged
all of us down with you.


00:53:27.583 --> 00:53:30.836
Nikki, just let it happen.


00:53:30.961 --> 00:53:35.424
Does this make you feel better?
Lay it all on me. I'm the fuck-up.


00:53:35.549 --> 00:53:39.636
Mum knows it. Dad knew it.
It's never you. It's always me.


00:53:39.761 --> 00:53:42.973
It is always you. I wasn't given
the room to make mistakes.


00:53:43.098 --> 00:53:46.351
- That room was filled with yours.
- I just wanted you to have fun.


00:53:46.476 --> 00:53:49.396
Bullshit. You wanted me to act like you


00:53:49.521 --> 00:53:54.860
cos if there's two of us it would make
you seem less of a disappointment.


00:53:54.985 --> 00:53:58.155
It must be nice to have your life
so together.


00:53:59.114 --> 00:54:01.200
Dad would be proud.


00:54:16.757 --> 00:54:20.260
What's up? You all right?


00:54:20.385 --> 00:54:23.972
- How you doing?
- I'm all right.


00:54:29.228 --> 00:54:32.064
You know, er...


00:54:32.189 --> 00:54:35.400
when our Dad got sick...


00:54:36.944 --> 00:54:40.614
...I knew Matt was pissed at me
for bailing,


00:54:40.739 --> 00:54:43.659
but I just didn't know what to do.


00:54:46.745 --> 00:54:51.667
After he died, I tried to make it up
to him. I tried to be around more.


00:54:53.836 --> 00:54:57.005
I just didn't know
he hated me so much.


00:54:57.130 --> 00:54:59.925
He doesn't hate you
as much as he thinks he does.


00:55:00.050 --> 00:55:04.054
- All evidence to the contrary.
- He loves you, John.


00:55:04.179 --> 00:55:09.726
He's here for you.
Mr Responsible skipped school,


00:55:09.852 --> 00:55:14.147
a week away from his finals, just to
spend a weekend with his big brother.


00:55:16.191 --> 00:55:19.278
- He can't say no to you.
- Yeah, look where it got him.


00:55:19.403 --> 00:55:22.072
None of this is your fault.


00:55:22.197 --> 00:55:24.741
You'll get through this.


00:55:24.867 --> 00:55:28.078
Besides, you're a hard guy
to stay angry at.


00:55:28.203 --> 00:55:30.080
- Yeah?
- Yeah.


00:55:30.205 --> 00:55:33.333
Even I don't hate you
quite as much as I used to.


00:55:34.376 --> 00:55:36.753
"Quite. "


00:55:38.839 --> 00:55:41.508
I really love him, you know.


00:55:41.633 --> 00:55:43.927
I know.


00:55:44.052 --> 00:55:46.680
I'm glad.


00:55:52.227 --> 00:55:54.104
- Hey.
- Want a sip?


00:55:54.229 --> 00:55:55.898
Uh-huh.


00:55:56.023 --> 00:56:00.402
Your uncle had
very eclectic musical tastes.


00:56:00.527 --> 00:56:02.821
That's putting it nicely.


00:56:02.946 --> 00:56:05.032
- Thank you.
- Cheers.


00:56:07.242 --> 00:56:10.370
Hey. You're gonna be fine.


00:56:14.291 --> 00:56:16.710
I feel awful.


00:56:16.835 --> 00:56:19.630
Why? You guys have been wanting
to do that for years.


00:56:19.755 --> 00:56:22.841
(Sara) You'll both recover.
(Matt) I hope so.


00:56:22.966 --> 00:56:25.511
- You ready to turn this mother out?
- (Sara) Yes!


00:56:25.636 --> 00:56:28.013
- Ready?
- (Matt) Come on, Mr DJ.


00:56:28.138 --> 00:56:30.766
(Blues music cuts out)


00:56:30.891 --> 00:56:34.770
(John) The fuse?
- Yeah. I'll get it. I know where it is.


00:56:34.895 --> 00:56:38.440
- (Matt) I'll come with you.
- No, no. Relax, relax.


00:56:38.565 --> 00:56:41.443
Each of you has your job.
You're the future doctor -


00:56:41.568 --> 00:56:43.987
smart and calm under pressure.


00:56:44.112 --> 00:56:46.907
You're the Eagle Scout
in black sheep's clothing -


00:56:47.032 --> 00:56:49.368
quick with a weapon
and handy with a sea plane.


00:56:49.493 --> 00:56:53.622
You're the perky, athletic one -
very randy to have around.


00:56:53.747 --> 00:56:58.460
And you... you look incredibly sexy
in a bikini.


00:56:58.585 --> 00:57:01.547
<i>Now where does all that leave moi?</i>


00:57:02.589 --> 00:57:05.592
I'm the one who knows
where the fuse box is.


00:57:08.679 --> 00:57:11.139
(Sara) He's in need of psychiatric help.


00:57:20.983 --> 00:57:24.027
(Creaking)


00:57:28.031 --> 00:57:30.117
(Metal can clatters)


00:57:31.618 --> 00:57:33.328
(Laughs)


00:57:33.453 --> 00:57:38.041
Why have they always gotta put
the fuse box in the basement? Damn.


00:57:41.044 --> 00:57:44.006
O... k.


00:57:46.550 --> 00:57:49.136
(Blues record starts again)


00:57:51.054 --> 00:57:52.931
(Laughs)


00:57:53.056 --> 00:57:54.975
Oh!


00:58:05.569 --> 00:58:08.405
You're mine, baby.


00:58:08.530 --> 00:58:10.407
(Music stops)


00:58:10.532 --> 00:58:13.702
Oh! You gotta be kidding me.


00:58:13.827 --> 00:58:16.830
(Cans clatter)


00:58:16.955 --> 00:58:19.041
(Laughs)


00:58:19.166 --> 00:58:22.127
Almost, baby.


00:58:22.252 --> 00:58:24.046
(Metallic rattle)


00:58:56.161 --> 00:58:59.414
(Low growl)


00:59:00.040 --> 00:59:01.124
(Dog snarls)


00:59:01.250 --> 00:59:05.003
(Noah screams)


00:59:07.214 --> 00:59:08.257
Stay with Sara.


00:59:15.305 --> 00:59:16.932
No!


00:59:23.021 --> 00:59:24.481
(Barking)


00:59:24.606 --> 00:59:27.025
Matt, slide that over here!


00:59:31.363 --> 00:59:34.908
(Sara) They're coming
through the door, Nikki! Hurry!


00:59:36.034 --> 00:59:38.912
Come on, come on!
Come on, hurry up!


00:59:41.957 --> 00:59:45.752
(John) Get Sara and get upstairs now!
(Matt) Get upstairs!


00:59:46.253 --> 00:59:49.173
(Nikki) Get upstairs!
(Matt) Get to the attic!


00:59:57.055 --> 00:59:58.515
Oh no!


01:00:13.155 --> 01:00:14.656
(Sara) Hurry up!


01:00:15.741 --> 01:00:17.492
(Nikki) Matt!


01:00:25.292 --> 01:00:26.335
(Nikki) Grab this!


01:00:31.298 --> 01:00:33.634
- (Nikki) Ok?
- Let's go, let's go!


01:00:39.431 --> 01:00:41.850
(Nikki) Hurry!
(John) Let's go!


01:00:55.697 --> 01:00:57.783
(John) Get the rope!


01:01:03.914 --> 01:01:07.835
(All out of breath)


01:01:10.504 --> 01:01:13.924
- (Nikki) You Ok?
- My shoulder.


01:01:14.049 --> 01:01:17.052
Oh, my God! You got bitten!


01:01:21.431 --> 01:01:23.392
(Snarling)


01:01:32.317 --> 01:01:35.070
(Howling)


01:01:45.163 --> 01:01:47.666
(Thunderclap)


01:01:50.377 --> 01:01:53.130
(Dog howls)


01:02:34.171 --> 01:02:37.257
None of this seems real.


01:02:37.382 --> 01:02:40.761
I can't believe that Noah is dead.


01:02:46.850 --> 01:02:51.313
Ok, look, we'll get out of here.
We'll get you guys to a doctor,


01:02:52.648 --> 01:02:55.984
Whatever it is,
they're gonna figure it out.


01:02:58.237 --> 01:03:00.739
(Whispers) Go away!


01:03:05.244 --> 01:03:07.204
- Hey, Sara, please...
- Get off me!


01:03:22.010 --> 01:03:24.721
- I'm so sorry.
- That's Ok.


01:03:24.847 --> 01:03:27.808
- You know I didn't mean that.
- That's Ok. Come here.


01:03:29.393 --> 01:03:32.771
(Sara) I'm sorry.
(John) I'm gonna get you out of here.


01:03:32.896 --> 01:03:35.607
- I promise.
- Ok.


01:03:35.732 --> 01:03:38.110
I just don't feel right.


01:03:39.778 --> 01:03:41.864
(John) I know.


01:03:45.993 --> 01:03:47.870
(John) You'll be all right.


01:03:51.456 --> 01:03:52.958
Johnny.


01:04:03.218 --> 01:04:05.304
AMCS.


01:04:06.597 --> 01:04:10.684
Army Mountain Combat School,
that's who leased the compound.


01:04:10.809 --> 01:04:15.272
- So they were training attack dogs?
- Could be experiments that went wrong.


01:04:15.397 --> 01:04:18.150
Why would Uncle Frank
have these papers?


01:04:21.069 --> 01:04:24.406
Uncle Frank wouldn't be involved
with something like this.


01:04:24.531 --> 01:04:28.285
- He was an animal rights activist.
- (John) keep telling yourself that.


01:04:28.410 --> 01:04:31.955
They probably told him what
he told me - that the dogs got rabies,


01:04:32.080 --> 01:04:35.959
it spread, and that's why
they had to put them all down.


01:04:36.084 --> 01:04:38.170
Well, they missed a few.


01:05:18.836 --> 01:05:21.880
- (Matt) Clear?
- (Whispers) Yeah, we're good.


01:05:37.104 --> 01:05:40.566
You guys get in the room.
Stay there.


01:05:43.360 --> 01:05:45.779
- Be careful.
- I will.


01:05:47.823 --> 01:05:49.908
(Flies buzzing)


01:06:11.680 --> 01:06:14.224
What's that smell?


01:06:14.391 --> 01:06:16.476
They've marked their territory.


01:06:17.519 --> 01:06:21.607
We're the ones trespassing now.


01:06:24.067 --> 01:06:25.777
(Door opens)


01:06:31.783 --> 01:06:33.952
You ready for this?


01:06:34.870 --> 01:06:38.081
No. You?


01:06:38.207 --> 01:06:40.292
No.


01:06:54.890 --> 01:06:57.518
Jesus, Matt. Matt!


01:07:00.062 --> 01:07:02.773
What is he doing? Is he insane?


01:07:04.191 --> 01:07:06.276
(Sara) He's not afraid.


01:07:10.072 --> 01:07:12.157
So sad.


01:07:14.576 --> 01:07:17.746
I've waited ten years
for him to notice me.


01:07:17.871 --> 01:07:20.582
What are you talking about?


01:07:22.125 --> 01:07:24.503
It feels over.


01:07:24.670 --> 01:07:27.798
It's not over. Don't talk like that.


01:07:51.530 --> 01:07:53.073
Pop the clutch!


01:07:56.493 --> 01:07:58.161
Shit!


01:07:58.287 --> 01:07:59.997
(Howling and barking)


01:08:07.588 --> 01:08:09.631
Come on, Mattie.


01:08:09.798 --> 01:08:11.925
Come on, Mattie!


01:08:15.137 --> 01:08:18.390
- Give me the bow.
- Here.


01:08:32.029 --> 01:08:34.406
Heads up, Mattie!


01:08:48.504 --> 01:08:50.881
(John) Come on, come on.


01:08:53.383 --> 01:08:55.594
We need more speed.


01:08:57.971 --> 01:08:59.223
(John) Hold on!


01:09:04.311 --> 01:09:06.688
Better work this time!


01:09:16.490 --> 01:09:18.283
(Engine starts)


01:09:36.635 --> 01:09:39.555
- Cool.
- Piece of cake.


01:09:42.307 --> 01:09:43.767
(Engine whines)


01:09:51.191 --> 01:09:53.652
They don't like the noise.


01:10:15.299 --> 01:10:17.342
Let's go!


01:10:18.969 --> 01:10:22.723
I don't think I'm gonna make
those finals, Johnny.


01:10:25.767 --> 01:10:27.644
Shit!


01:10:33.609 --> 01:10:35.152
Hold on to him!


01:10:38.197 --> 01:10:39.907
(Dog yelps)


01:10:53.295 --> 01:10:56.465
Sara won't come down.
You've gotta help.


01:10:56.632 --> 01:10:58.467
I got it, Mattie.


01:10:58.634 --> 01:11:00.511
- I tried everything.
- Get in.


01:11:01.845 --> 01:11:04.515
Sara!


01:11:05.557 --> 01:11:07.351
- Sara.
- Go away.


01:11:07.476 --> 01:11:09.102
- No.
- Get out!


01:11:09.269 --> 01:11:10.729
- No!
- I won't make it.


01:11:10.854 --> 01:11:13.607
I don't care! Get up! On your feet!


01:11:13.774 --> 01:11:15.234
(Dog growls)


01:11:16.527 --> 01:11:19.821
Get out of my house!


01:11:19.988 --> 01:11:22.658
- John, out the window!
- I'm not leaving!


01:11:22.824 --> 01:11:26.453
You understand?
If I break eye contact, it's over.


01:11:26.620 --> 01:11:28.872
I will be right behind you.


01:11:30.749 --> 01:11:33.335
- Gone?
- Yeah.


01:11:37.047 --> 01:11:39.132
(Screams)


01:11:51.728 --> 01:11:53.397
You Ok?


01:11:55.148 --> 01:11:56.733
(Screams)


01:11:57.442 --> 01:11:58.485
Sara!


01:12:00.112 --> 01:12:04.366
(Creaking)


01:12:07.995 --> 01:12:10.038
- Sara!
- (Matt) No, no.


01:12:13.041 --> 01:12:15.085
- (John) No!
- Come on!


01:12:51.288 --> 01:12:53.373
(Barking)


01:13:10.766 --> 01:13:13.352
(Matt) That fence didn't used
to be here.


01:13:15.354 --> 01:13:17.439
We'll break through it with the car.


01:13:17.564 --> 01:13:22.027
What if the fence is the only thing
standing between us and those dogs?


01:13:22.152 --> 01:13:24.530
That's true.


01:13:24.655 --> 01:13:28.283
(John) Ok... Ok,
but we'll leave the car running.


01:13:29.535 --> 01:13:32.704
If we turn it off, we don't know
if it'll start again.


01:13:32.829 --> 01:13:35.123
The car's not gonna
get us off this island.


01:13:35.249 --> 01:13:39.294
Well, if we need to,
it'll get us the hell out of here.


01:13:39.419 --> 01:13:41.672
Come on.


01:13:43.215 --> 01:13:47.469
(John) There's gotta be a radio here.
(Matt) It's no good if there's no power.


01:13:48.804 --> 01:13:51.849
- Look.
- (Matt) Solar panel.


01:13:52.891 --> 01:13:56.311
- We could hook onto that, right?
- Yeah.


01:14:07.239 --> 01:14:11.118
- Were you ever here?
- (Matt) No, not inside.


01:14:12.661 --> 01:14:15.163
Looks like an attack-protection suit.


01:14:36.643 --> 01:14:38.729
What the hell is all this stuff?


01:14:40.981 --> 01:14:45.652
This was not a training facility.
Something else was going on here.


01:14:47.237 --> 01:14:49.781
They weren't training anything.


01:14:49.907 --> 01:14:55.037
They were genetically redesigning them.
They were playing God.


01:14:55.162 --> 01:14:57.456
No!


01:15:02.002 --> 01:15:04.129
Let's keep moving.


01:15:14.014 --> 01:15:16.308
Here's a radio.


01:15:18.185 --> 01:15:19.853
No power.


01:15:19.978 --> 01:15:23.065
All right, how do we hook in
to the solar power?


01:15:23.190 --> 01:15:25.943
The batteries have to be
around here somewhere.


01:15:27.611 --> 01:15:29.863
(John) Down here.


01:15:38.539 --> 01:15:40.666
- Batteries.
- All right, good.


01:15:40.791 --> 01:15:43.126
I'm gonna check the main first.


01:15:44.795 --> 01:15:46.964
Hit the breaker.


01:15:48.841 --> 01:15:51.635
These batteries
are never gonna charge.


01:15:52.803 --> 01:15:54.680
They're too rusted. Look.


01:15:54.805 --> 01:15:58.475
No, they're the old lead-acid kind.
They'll hold a charge forever.


01:15:58.600 --> 01:16:02.354
Positive to positive.
Negative to negative. Just like a car.


01:16:03.856 --> 01:16:05.482
You good?


01:16:08.944 --> 01:16:11.280
- Nice.
- (John) Right.


01:16:16.660 --> 01:16:18.745
(Panel beeps and machine beeps)


01:16:18.871 --> 01:16:20.956
How do you know all this?


01:16:21.081 --> 01:16:25.127
You'd be surprised what an irresponsible
fuck-up can pick up over the years.


01:16:25.252 --> 01:16:27.713
(John) Ok, here we go.


01:16:28.881 --> 01:16:30.632
(Matt) Does it Work?


01:16:30.757 --> 01:16:33.802
- It's dead.
- Still no signal.


01:16:33.927 --> 01:16:36.513
Give me that cell phone.
Open the back.


01:16:36.638 --> 01:16:40.100
We can hook up this phone
to the radio tower.


01:16:40.225 --> 01:16:43.896
It's a giant antenna. By itself,
a cell gives you two, three miles,


01:16:44.021 --> 01:16:48.692
but a tower like that gives you
over 100. We attach the cell phone...


01:16:48.817 --> 01:16:52.196
here to the radio antenna.


01:16:53.780 --> 01:16:57.826
- (Phone beeps)
- Shit. No signal.


01:16:57.951 --> 01:17:02.247
Wait a minute, guys. Look right there,
on the radio tower.


01:17:02.372 --> 01:17:04.499
- There's a cable detached.
- I'll go.


01:17:04.625 --> 01:17:07.920
- We gotta stick together.
- I'll go.


01:17:08.045 --> 01:17:12.466
You guys stay here. Once I connect
the cables, you're gonna see this signal.


01:17:12.591 --> 01:17:18.388
When you see the signal, you wanna
turn on the antenna amplifier here.


01:17:18.514 --> 01:17:20.265
All right.


01:17:22.226 --> 01:17:24.686
Hey... Be careful.


01:17:24.811 --> 01:17:27.439
We're gonna get outta here.


01:17:45.666 --> 01:17:50.420
What's wrong?
Baby, calm down, sit down.


01:17:55.175 --> 01:17:57.344
It's just...


01:18:00.556 --> 01:18:03.141
What happened to Sara
is gonna happen to me.


01:18:03.267 --> 01:18:06.812
Matt, don't talk like that.
You're gonna drive yourself crazy.


01:18:17.322 --> 01:18:19.825
What's wrong?


01:18:19.950 --> 01:18:22.035
What?


01:18:22.160 --> 01:18:24.037
They're inside.


01:18:24.162 --> 01:18:26.498
What are you talking about?


01:18:27.541 --> 01:18:29.835
For the dogs to survive
being put down


01:18:29.960 --> 01:18:32.212
they would've had
to find a way to escape.


01:18:32.337 --> 01:18:36.049
If they found a way out
of the compound...


01:18:36.175 --> 01:18:38.385
They found their way back in.


01:18:41.680 --> 01:18:42.848
John.


01:18:58.822 --> 01:19:00.991
(Antenna buzzes)


01:19:08.832 --> 01:19:10.542
Argh!


01:19:16.965 --> 01:19:18.634
Oh, my God!


01:19:32.189 --> 01:19:35.692
(Barking)


01:20:00.551 --> 01:20:02.261
(Screaming)


01:20:21.113 --> 01:20:24.241
(Coughs)


01:21:15.000 --> 01:21:17.628
Give Cujo my best.


01:21:21.131 --> 01:21:22.883
(Screaming)


01:21:28.597 --> 01:21:31.225
Nikki!


01:21:31.350 --> 01:21:33.227
- Nikki!
- No!


01:21:34.603 --> 01:21:37.481
Stop it! Listen! Listen to me!


01:21:37.606 --> 01:21:40.400
There is a boat on the other side
of this fence!


01:21:40.526 --> 01:21:42.611
It's our only way out!


01:21:42.736 --> 01:21:46.114
We're not getting off this island, John!


01:22:14.518 --> 01:22:16.228
(Crash of metal)


01:22:19.314 --> 01:22:21.692
Need a ride?


01:22:25.445 --> 01:22:29.116
- I thought you were dead.
- Any ideas?


01:22:29.241 --> 01:22:30.492
Hang on!


01:22:42.546 --> 01:22:44.715
(Engine revs)


01:22:57.519 --> 01:22:59.605
Come on!


01:23:02.024 --> 01:23:03.901
- You Ok?
- Yeah.


01:23:07.613 --> 01:23:08.655
Go!


01:23:17.497 --> 01:23:19.958
John, get the boat started.


01:23:21.877 --> 01:23:23.962
Jump on!


01:23:53.075 --> 01:23:55.577
What do you think's gonna happen
to you guys?


01:23:59.039 --> 01:24:01.708
Find a doctor that can cure it.


01:24:03.126 --> 01:24:05.796
- What if he can't?
- He has to.


01:24:16.807 --> 01:24:19.142
I need some sleep.


01:24:31.446 --> 01:24:32.739
(Snarl)

